"[2212.14685] Irreducible subcube partitions (https://accelresearching.com/accel-zinc-picolinate-50mg/?_=%2Fabs%2F2212.14685%23nLw79nwZb1b3uPkZUsgpm5M%3D)\nciteturn6search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.8 years ago; Crawled: last month; [Submitted on 30 Dec 2022 (v1), last revised 8 Sep 2026 (this version, v4)] ... We study extremal properties of tight irreducible subcube partitions: minimal size, minimal weight, maximal number of points, maximal size, and maximal minimum dimension.\n\n# Mathematics > Combinatorics\n\n[Submitted on 30 Dec 2022 (v1), last revised 8 Sep 2026 (this version, v4)]\n\n# Title:Irreducible subcube partitions\n\nAuthors:Yuval Filmus, Edward Hirsch, Sascha Kurz, Ferdinand Ihringer, Artur Riazanov, Alexander Smal, Marc Vinyals\n\nView a PDF of the paper titled Irreducible subcube partitions, by Yuval Filmus and 6 other authors\n\nView PDF HTML (experimental)\n\n> Abstract:A \\emph{subcube partition} is a partition of the Boolean cube $\\{0,1\\}^n$ into subcubes. A subcube partition is irreducible if the only sub-partitions whose union is a subcube are singletons and the entire partition. A subcube partition is tight if it \"mentions\" all coordinates. We study extremal properties of tight irreducible subcube partitions: minimal size, minimal weight, maximal number of points, maximal size, and maximal minimum dimension. We also consider the existence of homogeneous tight irreducible subcube partitions, in which all subcubes have the same dimensions. We additionally study subcube partitions of $\\{0,\\dots,q-1\\}^n$, and partitions of $\\mathbb{F}_2^n$ into affine subspaces, in both cases focusing on the minimal size. Our constructions and computer experiments lead to several conjectures on the extremal values of the aforementioned properties.\n\nComments:  | 37 pages; updated with a refutation of some of the conjectures\nSubjects:  | Combinatorics (math.CO)\nCite as:  | arXiv:2212.14685 [math.CO]\n   | (or arXiv:2212.14685v4 [math.CO] for this version)\n   | https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2212.14685 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nRelated DOI (Digital Object Identifier):  | https://doi.org/10.37236/11862 DOI(s) linking to related resources\n\n## Submission history\n\nFrom: Yuval Filmus [view email]\n[v1] Fri, 30 Dec 2022 13:16:19 UTC (34 KB)\n[v2] Tue, 17 Jan 2023 16:36:56 UTC (41 KB)\n[v3] Fri, 18 Aug 2023 15:42:53 UTC (41 KB)\n[v4] Tue, 8 Sep 2026 15:12:12 UTC (43 KB)--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNote on polychromatic coloring of hereditary hypergraph families II (https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.24412)\nciteturn6academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Date: Mon Apr 27 12:37:56 2026\n\nWe extend a recent construction concerning polychromatic colorings of hereditary hypergraph families.\nTitle: Note on polychromatic coloring of hereditary hypergraph families II\nAuthors: Dömötör Pálvölgyi\nDate: Mon Apr 27 12:37:56 2026\n\nWe extend a recent construction concerning polychromatic colorings of hereditary hypergraph families. For every integer $h\\ge 4$ we construct a $(2h-1)$-uniform hypergraph which has no polychromatic $3$-coloring, but all of whose $h$-heavy restricted subhypergraphs are $2$-colorable. Together with the previously known case $h=3$, this gives examples with uniformity $2h-1$ for every $h\\ge 3$. The construction is based on complements of suitable $h$-uniform hypergraphs on $3h-1$ vertices. For $h\\ge 9$ we prove existence by a simple probabilistic argument; the remaining cases $4\\le h\\le 8$ are certified by a short exhaustive computer check, whose fully reproducible description and source code are included in the appendix.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNote on polychromatic coloring of hereditary hypergraph families II | Cool Papers - Immersive Paper Discovery (https://papers.cool/arxiv/2604.24412)\nciteturn6search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; We extend a recent construction concerning polychromatic colorings of hereditary hypergraph families. ... Publish: 2026-04-27 12:37:56 UTC\n# 2604.24412\n\nTotal: 1\n\n## #1 Note on polychromatic coloring of hereditary hypergraph families II [PDF^{}] [Copy] [Kimi^{}] [REL]\n\nAuthor: Dömötör Pálvölgyi\n\nWe extend a recent construction concerning polychromatic colorings of hereditary hypergraph families. For every integer $h\\ge 4$ we construct a $(2h-1)$-uniform hypergraph which has no polychromatic $3$-coloring, but all of whose $h$-heavy restricted subhypergraphs are $2$-colorable. Together with the previously known case $h=3$, this gives examples with uniformity $2h-1$ for every $h\\ge 3$. The construction is based on complements of suitable $h$-uniform hypergraphs on $3h-1$ vertices. For $h\\ge 9$ we prove existence by a simple probabilistic argument; the remaining cases $4\\le h\\le 8$ are certified by a short exhaustive computer check, whose fully reproducible description and source code are included in the appendix.\n\nSubjects: Combinatorics , Discrete Mathematics\n\nPublish: 2026-04-27 12:37:56 UTC--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDocument downloaded from http://www.elsevier.es, day 21/01/2026. This copy is for personal use. Any transmission of this document by any media or format is strictly prohibited. (https://multimedia.elsevier.es/PublicationsMultimediaV1/file/00017310/addon/S0001731009719192/S300/en/103v100n07a13140526pdf001_2.pdf)\nciteturn6search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago; Document downloaded from http://www.elsevier.es, day 21/01/2026. ... Atypical polychromatic pigmentary lesion with irregular ... patients with hereditary retinoblastoma.7,8 Cases have\nDocument downloaded from http://www.elsevier.es, day 21/01/2026. This copy is for personal use. Any transmission of this document by any media or format is strictly prohibited.\nDocument downloaded from http://www.elsevier.es, 